  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "When accessing the /fcr:fixity endpoint for binary resources, very large files can take a very long time to run – in excess of 60-90 seconds. This seems unusually slow, especially since I can reproduce the problem on a well-resourced test system under no load. I’m seeing the same behavior in two different storage configurations, so I don’t think the problem is specifically related to my disk setup.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "You can download the ~1.3GB flac audio file that first led me to discover the issue here:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://digital.library.villanova.edu/files/vudl:358843/MASTER"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://digital.library.villanova.edu/files/vudl:358843/MASTER",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "You should be able to upload this as a binary to Fedora and then add /fcr:fixity to the binary’s URL in order to see the problem in action. I’ll be interested to hear if this performs significantly better for others!",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Thank you!",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
